From: Tilo <noreply@tilo.so>
Subject: [PATCH] oci: copy a local repository's layers by their objects

`cfsctl oci copy --from` between two repositories on this machine sent each
layer through GetLayer and PutLayer: the source wrote the layer out as tar
around its objects, and the destination read that tar back, hashed all of it
for the diff ID and wrote a new splitstream. A layer's splitstream already
names its objects by their fs-verity digests, so when both repositories use
one hash type the layers the destination lacks are now copied as they are
stored: the splitstreams and the objects they name, on several threads, with
no content hashed in userspace. The destination's kernel measures each copied
object as it enables fs-verity, and an object that measures differently from
its name fails the copy. The varlink copy then finds the layers there and
writes only the manifest and config.
---
--- a/crates/composefs-oci/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/composefs-oci/src/lib.rs
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 pub(crate) mod delta;
 pub mod image;
 pub mod layer;
+pub mod layer_copy;
 pub mod layer_sync;
 pub mod layer_transport;
 pub mod oci_image;
--- a/crates/composefs-ctl/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/composefs-ctl/src/lib.rs
@@ -1972,6 +1972,37 @@
                     .map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!("OpenRepository failed on destination: {e:?}"))?
                     .handle;
 
+                // Two repositories of one hash type on this machine: the layers the
+                // destination lacks are copied as their splitstreams and the objects
